        // if n is not divisible by 3, then it cannot be a power of three
        return n == 1;
    }
}

This function first checks if n is less than or equal to zero, since powers of three are positive integers greater than zero. If n is negative, we can't have a power of three, so we immediately return false.

Next, we use a loop to repeatedly divide n by 3 until it becomes 1. This means that every time we divide n by 3, we're effectively reducing its value by half. We continue this process until n becomes 1, at which point we know that n must be a power of three.

Finally, we return true if n was reduced to 1 after the loop completes, and false otherwise.

